<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Velletri</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Velitrae</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Velletri is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alban-hills">Alban Hills</a> south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. As Velitrae it was a Volscian town that Rome colonised several times in the 5th and 4th centuries BCE; a bronze tablet found there is the main surviving text in the Volscian language. It was the home of the family of Gaius Octavius, father of the emperor Augustus.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/velletri.jpg" alt="Velletri" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Deblu68 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Velletri.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
